{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.gram_weighted_qvalue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gram_weighted_qvalue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Fin"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gram_weighted_qvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gram_weighted_qvalue","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L47-L142","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Proposition.**\n*Let $\\mathcal{G}_{\\mathrm{par}} = \\mathcal{G}(t_0, \\ldots, t_{A-1})$\nbe the typed Garside element\n([typed Garside element](#def:typed-garside-element)) of the parent\nnucleus in $H_A(q)$, and let $G$ be the Gram matrix\n$G_{ij} = \\mathrm{tr}_M(b_i \\cdot b_j)$ restricted to the NF\nsubspace spanned by $\\mathcal{G}_{\\mathrm{par}}$ and all conversion\ndaughters.  Then the $Q$-value for $\\beta^-$ decay is:*\n\n```tex\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:gram-weighted-qvalue}\n  Q(Z, N)\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\biggl(\n    \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\n    w_k^G \\;\\cdot\\; \\Delta_k\n  \\biggr)\n  \\,\\times\\, N \\,\\times\\, m_e\n\\end{equation}\n```\n\n*where:*\n\n1. *The sum runs over all $N$ neutrons in the parent\n   (all possible conversion channels).*\n\n2. *$\\mathcal{G}_{\\mathrm{dau}}^{(k)}$ is the typed Garside\n   element of the daughter obtained by converting neutron $k$\n   ($t_k = n \\mapsto p$), and*\n\n```tex\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:nf-reduction-cost}\n  \\Delta_k\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\lVert \\mathcal{G}_{\\mathrm{par}} \\rVert_1\n  \\;-\\;\n  \\lVert \\mathcal{G}_{\\mathrm{dau}}^{(k)} \\rVert_1\n\\end{equation}\n```\n\n   *is the NF reduction cost (change in $L^1$ norm of the\n   Gröbner--Shirshov normal form).*\n\n3. *The Gram weight for neutron $k$ is:*\n\n```tex\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:gram-weight}\n  w_k^G\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\frac{\n    \\lVert \\delta_k \\rVert_F\n  }{\n    \\sum_{j=0}^{N-1} \\lVert \\delta_j \\rVert_F\n  },\n  \\qquad\n  \\delta_k\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\mathcal{G}_{\\mathrm{par}} - \\mathcal{G}_{\\mathrm{dau}}^{(k)},\n  \\qquad\n  \\lVert \\delta_k \\rVert_F\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\sqrt{|\\delta_k \\cdot G \\cdot \\delta_k|}\n\\end{equation}\n```\n\n   *where $\\lVert \\cdot \\rVert_F$ is the Frobenius norm induced\n   by the Gram matrix.*\n\n**Inputs.**  The substrate parameter $q$\n(from $\\mathrm{Vol}(4_1)$ and $m_\\mu/m_e$) and the electron\nmass $m_e$.  No other parameters.\n\n## Structure of the formula\n\nThe $Q$-value has three factors:\n\n- **$\\Delta_k$** (NF reduction cost): measures how much algebraic\n  complexity the nucleus sheds when neutron $k$ converts.  The\n  daughter has fewer $\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The proposition is **named** below as a `def … : Prop` (pattern C):\n    `Δ` and `w` are opaque Gram-matrix-derived inputs, so the\n    three-part claim (formula, weights sum to one, weights non-negative)\n    is recorded as the conditional conjecture over the context rather than\n    discharged by a fake projection. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:gram-weighted-qvalue","label":"prop:gram-weighted-qvalue","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.w","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The Gram weight per channel `k`, indexed `Fin N → ℝ`; should sum to\n`1` (probability distribution over conversion channels). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.Δ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.Δ","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The NF-reduction cost per neutron-conversion channel `k`, indexed\n`Fin N → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.Q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.Q","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The `Q`-value of the `β⁻`-decay channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.m_e","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The electron mass `m_e : ℝ` (CODATA input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.N","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Neutron number `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.Z","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Proton number `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.q","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramWeightedQvalueContext","kind":"class","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/gram_weighted_qvalue.lean#L25-L45","doc":"Abstract context (inputs) for the `gram_weighted_qvalue` claim — the\nsubstrate parameter, the proton/neutron counts, the electron mass,\nthe `Q`-value, and the per-channel NF-reduction costs `Δ` and Gram\nweights `w`.  No field asserts a conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}